{"uttara":"dosalekha","kriya":"sadhana","nirnaya":{"sthana":"syan-nasti","artha":"in some respect it is not: a naya denied it, and no naya affirmed it"},"pramanya":{"marga":"kernel","saksin":"agda examined an emitted module and rejected it after 8 call(s); its own first error line is carried"},"hetu":"the kernel rejected every shape tried for (+ x (max x 0)) ≡ (* (s (s 0)) x)","nasta":["agda's first error line, which is the content of the rejection and is not paraphrased: x · (x + max x zero) != suc (x + max (suc x) zero) of type ℕ when checking that the expression cong (x ·_) (candidate x) has","the module that was rejected, which is the object the error is about: {-# OPTIONS --cubical --guardedness --safe --no-import-sorts #-}\nmodule Candidate where\nopen import Cubical.Foundations.Prelude\nopen import Cubical.Data.Nat using (ℕ ; zero ; suc ; _+_ ; _·_ ; _∸_)\nmax : ℕ → ℕ → ℕ\nmax a zero = a\nmax zero b = b\nmax (suc a) (suc b) = suc (max a b)\ncandidate : (x : ℕ) → (x + (max x zero)) ≡ ((suc (suc zero)) · x)\ncandidate x = refl\n","the distinction between `false` and `not provable in the shapes this emitter can write` — the emitter tries refl and then a fixed list of induction step shapes, and exhausting them is not a refutation"],"sesa":["if the statement needs a different induction, say which variable with `sadhya`","a rejection here is a fact about agda and this emitter; it is not a claim that the equation is false"],"pramana":["Certificate.hs — `Rejected` after n>0 agda calls means agda examined a module; `Untranslatable` with 0 means none was emitted"]}
